s on pH. Explicit iron and proton nodes balance sacrificial reductions. Surface thermal reactions may occur in UV-attenuated porewater despite strong ambient UV. Conditions are staged rather than asserted to work in one pot. Completeness is relative to the declared feedstock boundary, not a demonstrated synthesis of every feedstock from inorganic carbon. The unbalanced C6 degradation shortcut in the supplied review is excluded. The 21 molecule nodes and 14 reaction nodes exceed the requested minimum ranges to retain explicit redox accounting. A null environment_formed denotes an external feedstock or formation in multiple modeled environments.", "molecules": [{"id": "mol_001", "formula": "CO2", "iupac_name": "carbon dioxide", "common_name": "carbon dioxide", "inchi": "InChI=1S/CO2/c2-1-3", "role": "starting", "environment_formed": null}, {"id": "mol_002", "formula": "H2", "iupac_name": "dihydrogen", "common_name": "hydrogen", "inchi": "InChI=1S/H2/h1H", "role": "starting", "environment_formed": null}, {"id": "mol_003", "formula": "H2O", "iupac_name": "oxidane", "common_name": "water", "inchi": "InChI=1S/H2O/h1H2", "role": "starting", "environment_formed": null}, {"id": "mol_004", "formula": "C3H4O3", "iupac_name": "2-oxopropanoic acid", "common_name": "pyruvic acid; pyruvate reference form", "inchi": "InChI=1S/C3H4O3/c1-2(4)3(5)6/h1H3,(H,5,6)", "role": "hub_intermediate", "environment_formed": null}, {"id": "mol_005", "formula": "C2H2O3", "iupac_name": "2-oxoacetic acid", "common_name": "glyoxylic acid; glyoxylate reference form", "inchi": "InChI=1S/C2H2O3/c3-1-2(4)5/h1H,(H,4,5)", "role": "starting", "environment_formed": null}, {"id": "mol_006", "formula": "C4H4O5", "iupac_name": "2-oxobutanedioic acid", "common_name": "oxaloacetic acid; oxaloacetate reference form", "inchi": "InChI=1S/C4H4O5/c5-2(4(8)9)1-3(6)7/h1H2,(H,6,7)(H,8,9)", "role": "starting", "environment_formed": null}, {"id": "mol_007", "formula": "C5H6O6", "iupac_name": "2-hydroxy-4-oxopentanedioic aci