, "catalyst": "H+ through acid-catalyzed proton transfers", "aqueous": true, "other": "A separate acidic, water-rich geothermal stage is required after aminonitrile formation. Residence time and acidity must be established experimentally; ordinary ambient neutral water is not assumed to give rapid complete hydrolysis."}, "mechanism": "Both nitrile groups hydrate through amide-containing intermediates and ultimately become carboxylic acids. This is a lumped multistep node; the ordering of the two hydrolyses is unspecified. Reference balance: C5H7N3 + 4 H2O -> C5H9NO4 + 2 NH3.", "reasoning": "Patel et al. (2015) provide the supplied aminonitrile-precursor context. Nitrogen balance requires two ammonia equivalents, correcting the review's one-ammonia equation. The proposed warm acidic implementation is not established by that summary and is a key kinetic bottleneck. Incomplete amide hydrolysis, decomposition and glutamate cyclization can limit recovery; acidic solutions contain much of the released nitrogen as NH4+."}], "pathways": [{"pathway_id": "P1", "name": "Supplied pyruvate/glyoxylate with hydroxylamine completion", "description": "Begin at supplied C3 and C2 keto-acid feedstocks, construct the C5 skeleton, then use hydroxylamine and sacrificial iron. This is the direct organic-feedstock entry; the selective reduction in rxn_007 remains conditional.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_003", "rxn_006", "rxn_007", "rxn_008"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_007", "mol_009", "mol_010"]}, {"pathway_id": "P2", "name": "Supplied pyruvate/glyoxylate with ammonia completion", "description": "Use the same C5 carbon construction but replace hydroxylamine with ammonia and H2. Transfer to the proposed FeS-bearing reducing interface is required; its catalytic competence is unverified.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_003", "rxn_006", "rxn_007", "rxn_009"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_007", "mol_009", "mol_010"]}, {"pathway_id": "P3", "name": "CO2-derived pyruvate with hydroxylamine completion