arbon-carbon bond formation preceding decarboxylation; the preparative oxalomalate step remains conditional.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_004", "rxn_005", "rxn_006", "rxn_007", "rxn_008"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_008", "mol_007", "mol_010"]}, {"pathway_id": "P8", "name": "Aldol addition before oxaloacetate decarboxylation, ammonia completion", "description": "Pass through oxalomalate and the shared C5 keto-acid sequence, then use ammonia/H2. Both the oxalomalate preparative implementation and the final FeS/H2 step require validation.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_004", "rxn_005", "rxn_006", "rxn_007", "rxn_009"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_008", "mol_007", "mol_010"]}, {"pathway_id": "P9", "name": "Acrolein/HCN route through an accumulated cyanohydrin", "description": "Construct the nitrile-bearing aldehyde from acrolein and HCN, add a second cyanide to form the cyanohydrin, convert it through Strecker equilibria to the aminodinitrile, and hydrolyze both nitriles. The initial conjugate-cyanation selectivity and final hydrolysis are major unresolved bottlenecks.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_010", "rxn_011", "rxn_012", "rxn_014"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_019", "mol_020", "mol_021"]}, {"pathway_id": "P10", "name": "Acrolein/HCN route with direct Strecker capture", "description": "Construct the same nitrile-bearing aldehyde but expose it directly to ammonia and HCN rather than requiring prior cyanohydrin accumulation. Hydrolysis of the shared aminodinitrile yields racemic glutamate. This is an alternative entry within the Strecker family, not a tenth independently established family.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_010", "rxn_013", "rxn_014"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_019", "mol_021"]}], "hub_molecules": ["mol_001", "mol_002", "mol_003", "mol_004", "mol_005", "mol_006", "mol_007", "mol_010", "mol_012", "mol_013", "mol_014", "mol_015", "mol_016", "mol_018", "mol_019", "mol_021"], "convergence_points": [{"molecule_id": "mol_004", "incoming_reactions": ["rxn_001", "rxn